  "id": "COMPOUND:15186 - PROTEIN:1919",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a multi-step mechanism by which Neogitogenin may influence Wiskott-Aldrich syndrome protein (WASP). Neogitogenin is implicated in targeting Sucrose porin, which is a key component of the bacterial outer membrane. This porin is subsequently targeted by seco-plakortolide K and another compound, (1S,3R,4R,6R,7R,8S,9R,10R,13S,16R)-5,5,9,14-tetramethyltetracyclo[11.2.1.01,10.04,8]hexadec-14-ene-3,4,6,7,9,16-hexol, both of which are known to interact with WASP. The presence of multiple targets for Sucrose porin, along with the direct interaction of these compounds with WASP, indicates a potential pathway where Neogitogenin could modulate the activity of WASP through the regulation of its target proteins. The cumulative evidence supports a mechanistic link between Neogitogenin and WASP, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
